On Sunday 19 October 2003 20:40 Douglas Mendum wrote:

> In my current game I have a blessed greased very rusty very corroded
> +2
> long sword as my only weapon.  I also have a wand of cancellation, and
> I was wondering if I zapped the sword with it, would it just turn
> uncursed and still be damaged, or would it turn into an uncursed
> undamaged sword?

An uncursed +0 damaged greased sword. Cancellation removes any blessing,
curse and enchantment, but it does nothing about damage or
rustproofing.

You *can* unrust it by dipping it into oil, though. As it's very rusty
and very corroded, you'll need more than one application. Grease
doesn't work that way, as you've noticed.

If you've got a non-cursed scroll of enchant weapon, it's better to use
that to repair the sword (so it will be properly +2 again and rustproof
to boot) than to cancel and re-enchant it (which will make it +1 or +2
and still very rusty).

